SCOPE OF THE APACHE-2.0 GRANT — CODE ONLY (decision 2026-06-16)

The Apache-2.0 license covers ONLY the server code in this package. It does NOT
cover the Governancer **funnel-base corpus** that this server loads at runtime.

Any corpus loaded via the `FUNNEL_BASE_ROOT` environment variable — the curated,
lawyer-attested primary statutory text, the per-statute validation bundles, and
the validation-summary ledger that `validate_citation` cross-checks against — is a
SEPARATE dataset supplied by the operator. The corpus that Agonist Development AB
runs against this server is its own PROPRIETARY, ALL-RIGHTS-RESERVED dataset: it is
NOT distributed under Apache-2.0, NOT included in this package's published `files`,
and must NOT be redistributed.

Rationale: the curated/validated corpus + citation ledger is the defensible
asset; the server is a thin, replaceable loader. Open-sourcing the loader under a
permissive license maximises adoption (NLnet eligibility, governancer-foundation
OSS home) while the proprietary corpus preserves the moat. A downstream user who
takes this Apache-2.0 server still needs their own validated corpus to make
`validate_citation` / `get_statute` meaningful.
